{"id":"h19t3","name":"Ordered Conversion Funnel","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>events</b> has the columns <code>user_id</code>, <code>event_at</code> (timestamp) and <code>event_name</code> (<code>'view'</code>, <code>'cart'</code>, <code>'purchase'</code> or other names, which are ignored).</p>\n<p>The funnel of a user is built from their <b>first</b> <code>'view'</code>:</p>\n<ul><li>step 1 <code>view</code>: the user has a view (its time is <code>v</code>);</li>\n<li>step 2 <code>cart</code>: the user has a cart event <b>strictly after</b> <code>v</code> and at most 7 days after <code>v</code> (<code>event_at &lt;= v + 7 days</code>); the first such cart has the time <code>c</code>;</li>\n<li>step 3 <code>purchase</code>: the user has a purchase <b>strictly after</b> <code>c</code> and at most 7 days after <code>v</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>A cart or purchase that happened before the first view does not count, and a user without a view is not in the funnel at all.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return 3 rows with the columns <code>step</code> (1, 2, 3), <code>name</code> (<code>view</code>, <code>cart</code>, <code>purchase</code>), <code>users</code>, <code>pct_of_previous</code> (100 times users of this step divided by users of the previous step, rounded to 1 decimal; <code>NULL</code> for step 1 or when the previous step has 0 users) and <code>pct_of_first</code> (same against step 1, <code>NULL</code> when step 1 has 0 users), sorted by <code>step</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>events</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>user_id</th><th>event_at</th><th>event_name</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:10:00</td><td>cart</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:20:00</td><td>purchase</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>cart</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 08:05:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-03-08 08:00:00</td><td>cart</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-03-09 08:10:00</td><td>purchase</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2026-03-10 08:00:00</td><td>cart</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>cart</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2026-03-02 08:01:00</td><td>share</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2026-03-02 08:02:00</td><td>purchase</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2026-03-02 08:30:00</td><td>view</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2026-03-09 08:00:00</td><td>cart</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2026-03-09 08:00:00</td><td>purchase</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>step</th><th>name</th><th>users</th><th>pct_of_previous</th><th>pct_of_first</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>view</td><td>5</td><td>null</td><td>null</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>cart</td><td>3</td><td>60.0</td><td>60.0</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>purchase</td><td>1</td><td>33.3</td><td>20.0</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>events</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>step</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>users</code>, <code>pct_of_previous</code>, <code>pct_of_first</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["entonnoir ordonné","premier événement après un autre","fenêtre de 7 jours","pourcentages","jointures latérales"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>events</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 5 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>step</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>users</code>, <code>pct_of_previous</code>, <code>pct_of_first</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"events":{"columns":[["user_id","INT"],["event_at","TIMESTAMP"],["event_name","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","view"],[1,"2026-03-02 08:10:00","cart"],[1,"2026-03-02 08:20:00","purchase"],[2,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","cart"],[2,"2026-03-02 08:05:00","view"],[2,"2026-03-08 08:00:00","cart"],[2,"2026-03-09 08:10:00","purchase"],[3,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","view"],[3,"2026-03-10 08:00:00","cart"],[4,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","view"],[4,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","cart"],[4,"2026-03-02 08:01:00","share"],[5,"2026-03-02 08:02:00","purchase"],[6,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","view"],[6,"2026-03-02 08:30:00","view"],[6,"2026-03-09 08:00:00","cart"],[6,"2026-03-09 08:00:00","purchase"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["step","name","users","pct_of_previous","pct_of_first"],"rows":[[1,"view",5,null,null],[2,"cart",3,60.0,60.0],[3,"purchase",1,33.3,20.0]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"events":{"columns":[["user_id","INT"],["event_at","TIMESTAMP"],["event_name","TEXT"]],"rows":[[1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","cart"],[2,"2026-03-02 08:00:00","purchase"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["step","name","users","pct_of_previous","pct_of_first"],"rows":[[1,"view",0,null,null],[2,"cart",0,null,null],[3,"purchase",0,null,null]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}